    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d889">

                <pb facs="0850" n="746" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg746"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.11/1208.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Ambassador to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico City</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-02-28">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 28, 1913</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department’s No. 46, February 27, 2 p.m. I think the Department misinterpreted De
                    la Barra’s telegram owing to its involved statement. It was not intended to be
                    definite and conclusive but simply an expression of the good will with which he
                    has taken up his task.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
